<title>USA: Wall Street Journal starts California Journal.</title>
<headline>Wall Street Journal starts California Journal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Wall Street Journal, published by Dow Jones &amp; Co Inc, said on Wednesday it plans to introduce a California Journal on October 2.</p>
<p>The California version will have five additional pages for regional business and economic issues every Wednesday.</p>
<p>The paper said it has a circulation of 230,000 in the state.</p>
